-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THIS LICENCE COVERS

This MIT licence covers the code written for Analog Atlas: index.html, css/,
js/, scripts/, tests/, design/, serve.py, start.bat, config.example.js,
firmware/, the helper scripts in data/raw/mars_ez_extract/, and the pitch
code (pitch/promo.html, pitch/pixelcat.js, pitch/fix_webm.py,
pitch/deck/backgrounds.html and pitch/deck/build_deck.ps1).

The team-written data files (data/*.json) are shared under the same MIT terms.
The numbers in them are not ours: each value names the source it comes from
(NASA POWER, mission papers, NASA fact sheets and others). When you reuse a
value, cite that source.

It does NOT cover the third-party files below. They keep their own licences.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY FILES IN THIS FOLDER

- vendor/cesium/      CesiumJS, Apache License 2.0 (see vendor/cesium/LICENSE.md)
- vendor/pannellum/   Pannellum 2.5.7 by Matthew Petroff, MIT
                      (see vendor/pannellum/LICENSE)
- vendor/fonts/       IBM Plex Sans, IBM Plex Sans Condensed and IBM Plex Mono,
                      Copyright 2017 IBM Corp., SIL Open Font License 1.1
                      (see vendor/fonts/OFL.txt)
- data/raw/           values from public data services, saved by our scripts
                      without changing the numbers: NASA POWER answers,
                      elevation samples from Open-Meteo (Copernicus DEM) and
                      NASA Solar System Treks, and pixel values read from the
                      LRO Diviner polar maps (Diviner team, UCLA). This
                      includes data/raw/removed/ (sites taken out of the app).
                      The team's own notes there (mars_ez_research.json,
                      removed/README.txt, removed/terrain_summary.json,
                      moonbase/README.txt, moonbase/sources.json)
                      follow the data/*.json rule above. moonbase/sources.json
                      holds short exact quotes from the NASA and USGS pages it
                      links, kept as evidence for the values.

Satellite data measured from orbit (the "Measured from orbit" card and the
"Ground surface" temperature switch). Our files hold numbers derived from them;
when you reuse those numbers, keep these credits:
- data/lst.json, data/screening_lst.json, data/raw/lst/
                      NASA MODIS MOD21A2 (Terra) and MYD21A2 (Aqua) v061 land
                      surface temperature, NASA LP DAAC
                      (doi:10.5067/MODIS/MOD21A2.061,
                      doi:10.5067/MODIS/MYD21A2.061). CC0: NASA-led mission
                      data, per the NASA Earthdata data use guidance
                      (https://www.earthdata.nasa.gov/engage/open-data-services-software-policies/data-use-guidance).
- data/composition.json, data/screening_composition.json, data/raw/composition/
                      MODIS MOD21A2 v061 band-29 emissivity (as above, CC0).
                      Copernicus Sentinel-2 L2A surface reflectance
                      (doi:10.5270/S2_-742ikth), free, full and open under the
                      Copernicus Sentinel data legal notice:
                      "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data 2023-2024".
                      ASTER L1T v003 (NASA/METI/AIST/Japan Spacesystems and
                      U.S./Japan ASTER Science Team; NASA LP DAAC;
                      doi:10.5067/ASTER/AST_L1T.003), openly shared without
                      restriction under the EOSDIS Data Use and Citation
                      Guidance (its NASA Earthdata catalog page).
- data/emit.json      NASA EMIT L2B minerals and L2A masks, NASA LP DAAC
                      (doi:10.5067/EMIT/EMITL2BMIN.001, .002;
                      doi:10.5067/EMIT/EMITL2AMASK.002, .003). CC0 as above.

Map and elevation data for Discover Jordan (data/screening_jordan.json,
data/raw/screening/) and for the Jordan rock-type sources in
data/sites_meta.json. When you reuse these values, keep these credits:
- IGME5000 geological map: "IGME5000, © BGR, Hannover, 2005,
                      https://doi.org/10.25928/igme-5000, modified:
                      reclassified to Analog Atlas rock ids". Licence: GeoNutzV
                      (German federal licence for geodata),
                      https://sg.geodatenzentrum.de/web_public/gdz/lizenz/geonutzv.pdf
- Copernicus DEM GLO-90 (2021 release): "Produced using Copernicus
                      WorldDEM-90 (c) DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence
                      and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the
                      European Union and ESA; all rights reserved."
- Natural Earth 1:10m Admin 0 - Countries (Jordan's border): public domain.

Globe pictures (textures/), all public domain:
- earth.jpg   NASA Earth Observatory, Blue Marble Next Generation (Reto Stöckli)
- moon.jpg    NASA Scientific Visualization Studio, CGI Moon Kit (Ernie Wright);
              LRO LROC WAC colour mosaic, NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University
- mars.jpg    NASA/JPL/USGS Astrogeology Science Center, Viking MDIM 2.1
              (colorization by NASA Ames)
The Earth and Mars pictures were made smaller and the Moon picture was saved
as JPEG; data/assets.json gives the details.

Photos and panoramas (panoramas/). The photographer, source page and
licence of each photo are also in data/panoramas.json and are shown in the app
next to the photo. Unless a line says otherwise, the file is used unchanged
(for many Wikimedia Commons files, the smaller copy that Commons itself serves).
data/assets.json lists how each file was processed.

