If you share or reuse a CC BY or CC BY-SA photo, keep the credit and the
licence name, and say if you changed it. If you change a CC BY-SA photo, share
your changed version under the same licence.

Pitch material (pitch/): the deck (AnalogAtlas_CosmicCats.pptx, deck/bg/,
deck/preview/) and the promo videos (analog-atlas-pitch-promo30.webm,
analog-atlas-pitch-promo60.webm) use photos from panoramas/ that we changed:
cropped, darkened or colour-graded, with drawings added. Their credits are on
the slides and on the video end card. Some of these photos are CC BY-SA
(wadi-rum-day.jpg, harrat-usaykhim.jpg, qaidam-yardangs-mangya.jpg,
craters-of-the-moon-big-craters-spatter-cones.jpg), so if you share the deck
or a video, keep the credits and share it under CC BY-SA 4.0. The app
screenshots (pitch/shots/ and the deck) also show map imagery streamed at run
time (NASA GIBS, NASA Solar System Treks, Cesium ion); see the last section.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SHOWN IN THE APP BUT NOT STORED IN THIS FOLDER

- Google Street View views (places listed in data/streetview.json) are shown
  live through Google's own Maps embed. The imagery is (c) Google and its
  contributors (some views are photospheres by named people, credited in the
  app). It is never copied into this folder, and its use follows Google's
  terms.
- 3D tiles, terrain and imagery streamed at run time (Cesium ion: Cesium World
  Terrain, Bing Maps imagery, Cesium Moon and Cesium Mars; NASA GIBS; NASA
  Solar System Treks) are not part of this repository and follow their
  providers' terms. The app shows their credits on screen.
